---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Everything that is neither a privacy request nor a takedown.
const general = 'contact@bikes.pizza';
// Reports of content that should not be on the site, and takedown requests.
const removals = 'remove.post@bikes.pizza';
// The law these terms are read under. Set this to the state Pizza Predator
// LLC is organized in (for example "the State of Illinois").
const governingLaw = 'the State of New Mexico';
const updated = 'September 20, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use · bikes.pizza"
  description="The rules for using bikes.pizza, and for the photos, comments and messages members share."
>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-light tracking-wide text-ink">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted text-sm font-light">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-ink font-light leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <p>
          bikes.pizza is a place to share photographs of bicycles and pizza. These
          terms cover the bikes.pizza website and the bikes.pizza apps for iOS and
          Android (together, "the service"), all operated by Pizza Predator LLC
          ("we", "us").
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          By creating an account or using the service you agree to these terms and
          to our <a href="/privacy" class="text-spice hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
          If you do not agree, do not use the service.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          The short version: share your own photos of bikes and pizza, be decent to
          other members, and do not post anything objectionable. We have no
          tolerance for objectionable content or abusive members, and we remove
          both.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Who can use bikes.pizza</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You must be at least 13 years old to use the service, and old enough to
          agree to these terms where you live. If you are under 18, you may use the
          service only with the permission of a parent or guardian. You may not use
          the service if we have previously removed your account for breaking
          these terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Your account</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You are responsible for your account and for what is done with it. Keep
          your sign-in details to yourself, give us an email address you can be
          reached at, and tell us if you think someone else has got into your
          account. One person, one account: do not create accounts by automated
          means, and do not create a new account to get around a suspension or a
          block. Your username must not impersonate another person or organization
          and must itself follow the content rules below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Your content</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          "Your content" is anything you send to the service: photos, titles,
          descriptions, comments, reactions, messages, your username and what you
          put on your profile.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You keep ownership of your content. By sending it to the service you
          grant Pizza Predator LLC a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free,
          perpetual license to store, review, reproduce, resize, publish, and
          display it on bikes.pizza and in the bikes.pizza apps, and to show it in
          the course of promoting bikes.pizza. For a published post this license
          continues after your account is closed, because posts are kept as a
          lasting public archive; the{' '}
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-spice hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>{' '}
          explains what is kept and how to ask for a post to be removed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You promise that your content is yours to share: that you took the photo
          or otherwise hold the rights to it, that sharing it does not infringe
          anyone's copyright, trademark, privacy or other rights, and that it
          follows the content rules below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Content rules</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          There is no tolerance on bikes.pizza for objectionable content or for
          abusive behavior. You agree not to submit, post, or send anything that:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
          <li>is sexually explicit, pornographic, or obscene;</li>
          <li>is violent or gory, or threatens, incites, or glorifies violence;</li>
          <li>
            harasses, bullies, stalks, intimidates, or demeans anyone, or is hateful
            toward people because of their race, ethnicity, national origin,
            religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, disability, or
            medical condition;
          </li>
          <li>
            shows a person. bikes.pizza is about bicycles and pizza, and photos of
            people, including yourself, are not accepted;
          </li>
          <li>
            reveals anyone's private information, such as a home address, phone
            number, license plate, or identity document;
          </li>
          <li>
            exploits or endangers children in any way (see our{' '}
            <a href="/child-safety" class="text-spice hover:underline">child safety standards</a>);
          </li>
          <li>is illegal, or promotes illegal activity or the sale of regulated goods;</li>
          <li>infringes someone else's copyright, trademark, or other rights;</li>
          <li>
            is spam, advertising, a scam, or a repeated or off-topic post, or
            contains malware or links to it;
          </li>
          <li>is false or misleading in a way that could cause harm, or impersonates anyone.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">You also agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
          <li>contact a member who has blocked you or asked you to stop;</li>
          <li>
            collect other members' information, or scrape, crawl, or copy the
            service by automated means without our written permission;
          </li>
          <li>
            interfere with the service, probe or get around its security or its
            moderation, or use it to send anything harmful to others;
          </li>
          <li>use the service for any unlawful purpose.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Moderation and enforcement</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Photos are checked automatically when they are submitted and are
          published only after a person has reviewed them. Comments and messages
          are screened automatically, and a comment can be held for review. We may
          decline to publish a submission for any reason, and being on topic and
          within the rules does not entitle a submission to be published.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We may remove or hide any content, and suspend or close any account, at
          any time, with or without notice, if we believe these terms have been
          broken or that it is necessary to protect members, the service, or
          anyone else. Serious or repeated violations lead to permanent removal.
          We may report illegal content to the authorities.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We try to keep objectionable content off the service, but we cannot
          promise that you will never encounter any. Content comes from members,
          and they alone are responsible for it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Reporting and blocking</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If you see something that breaks these rules, report it. Every comment
          and every conversation has a Report action in its menu, and a comment
          reported by several members is hidden until a moderator has looked at it.
          To report a post, or anything else, write to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${removals}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{removals}</a>{' '}
          with a link. We review reports promptly, aiming to act within 24 hours,
          by removing the content and, where warranted, the member who posted it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          You can block another member from a conversation's menu. A blocked member
          can no longer message you, and you can turn off messages from other
          members altogether in your account settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Copyright complaints</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If you believe something on bikes.pizza infringes your copyright, write
          to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${removals}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{removals}</a>{' '}
          with a link to the content, a description of the work you say is
          infringed, your contact details, a statement that you believe in good
          faith the use is not authorized, and a statement that your notice is
          accurate and that you are the owner of the right or authorized to act for
          the owner. We remove infringing content and close the accounts of repeat
          infringers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">The shop</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The shop sells bikes.pizza merchandise. Orders, payment, shipping, and
          returns are handled through Shopify, and the terms and policies shown at
          checkout apply to your purchase. Prices and availability can change
          without notice, and we may refuse or cancel an order, in which case you
          are refunded.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Our content</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The bikes.pizza name, logo, design, software, and the content we write
          belong to Pizza Predator LLC or its licensors. Members' content belongs
          to the members who shared it. You may view and share links to the
          service for personal, non-commercial use; you may not copy, republish, or
          make commercial use of the service's content without permission from
          whoever owns it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Links and other services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The service links to and relies on services we do not run, such as
          Apple, Google, and Shopify. We are not responsible for them, and your use
          of them is governed by their own terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Leaving, and ending these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can stop using the service and delete your account at any time, from
          the Settings screen in the app or the account page on this website. We
          may suspend or end your access as described under "Moderation and
          enforcement", and we may change or discontinue the service, or any part
          of it, at any time. The sections of these terms that by their nature
          should outlast your account do so, including the license for published
          posts, the disclaimers, and the limits on liability.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of
          any kind, whether express or implied, including implied warranties of
          merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
          We do not promise that the service will be uninterrupted, secure, or
          free of errors, or that content on it is accurate. Nothing on
          bikes.pizza is advice about the safety of a bicycle, a component, a
          route, or a food.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the fullest extent the law allows, Pizza Predator LLC and its owners,
          employees, and agents are not liable for any indirect, incidental,
          special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data,
          profits, or goodwill, arising from your use of the service or from
          content or conduct of other members. Our total liability for any claim
          about the service is limited to the greater of 50 US dollars or the
          amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim arose. Some
          places do not allow some of these limits, so parts of this section may
          not apply to you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Indemnity</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If someone brings a claim against us because of your content or because
          you broke these terms, you agree to cover the losses and reasonable
          costs, including legal fees, that result, to the extent the law allows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Governing law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the United States and of{' '}
          {governingLaw}, without regard to conflict-of-law rules, and disputes
          are to be brought in the courts located there. If you are a consumer,
          this does not take away protections that the law of the place where you
          live gives you and that cannot be waived. If any part of these terms is
          found unenforceable, the rest stays in effect, and our not enforcing a
          term is not a waiver of it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If these terms change we will update the date at the top of this page.
          Substantial changes will be announced on the site. Continuing to use the
          service after a change means you accept the new terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-light text-ink">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Questions about these terms are welcome at{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${general}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{general}</a>.
          Reports of content that should not be here go to{' '}
          <a href={`mailto:${removals}`} class="text-spice hover:underline">{removals}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
